{
  "dom_id": "step-q105993",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y={x}^{2}+2?$",
  "worked_solution": "In general, the graph of $y={x}^{2}+k$ looks like the standard parabola $y={x}^{2}$ but translated $k$ units up. The vertex of $y={x}^{2}+k$ is located at $(0,k).$\n\nIn the given function $y={x}^{2}+2,$ we have $k=2.$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the parabola $y={x}^{2}$ after being translated $2$ units *up*. The vertex is located at $(0,2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14241402/assets/c6e9f0867c9b5c04ed1390b01ece62d1fb33673e1e17373a92b2b2d576aeae05.png)",
